    "bottomLine": "A friendly choice for interior or enclosed block where odor and fumes are a concern.",
    "description": "Seal-Once Nano+Poly is aimed at people who want a penetrating masonry sealer they can apply in a basement, garage or workshop without the smell of solvent products. It is a water-based formula that the maker says combines nano-scale particles that penetrate into the masonry with a polymer that adds a lightly protective layer near the surface. The label lists low VOCs and soap-and-water cleanup, which makes it easier to use in enclosed spaces and around living areas. On block, it reduces water absorption and helps with dusting and staining, and it is suitable for brick, concrete and stucco as well. It is lighter-duty than a dedicated silane-siloxane repellent on exposed exterior walls, and like other repellents it is not intended to hold back water pushed through a wall from wet soil. Very porous or split-face block may need more product than the headline coverage suggests. Owner feedback is generally positive on ease of use and odor. Expect roughly $50 to $80 a gallon at the time of writing."
